title Caravan respect -- the run after reads the ending it inherited
prompt Keaton set the autonomous loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the operator card and the itineraries, close any agent-closable red first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first and send it as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED -- %96, %97, %98, %99 each carry a proof line, and %99's wall (the harness prose scan) was seated last lap. No red books the allocation, so the constructive queue is open.
think The running thread is the correspondence arc in Caravan. The newest log's recommend names the next door exactly: a run that finds a closure standing should inherit a matter already ended rather than opening the whole correspondence afresh -- the shape mind wore for the forbearance five tiers down.
think Read the shape rather than recall it. conclude writes eleven bytes into plan.close for a run that has not started, and the arc had no rung that ever opens one. A note addressed forward is worth what the run receiving it does with it; nothing in the tree yet did anything with it.
think Named the rung respect. Grepped the whole caravan module: zero occurrences, so no collision with the arc's own prose. spare was the first candidate and lost on measurement -- bear.rye and five other rungs already spend spare with a different sense, and a name that reads two ways inside one module is a name that costs a reader.
think Modelled it on mind exactly, since mind is the arc's own inheritance shape: read the note the run before addressed forward, weigh the word standing in it rather than assuming one, weigh that word against the reader's own box where they wrote it, publish the mark, read the mark back, and only then take the inheritance down. The naming lands first so a run falling between the two leaves an ending standing for the next hand.
think Placed the call ahead of close_the_matter rather than after it. A closure is addressed forward, so the only honest moment to read one is before this run's own concluding writes a fresh one over it -- which is precisely where mind_the_impasse stands relative to hold_the_matter.
think The pair asks the concluding below to write nothing on either run. That was a correction mid-lap: with both plans concluding, the wire at the end of the lap carries a fresh closure and the taking-down of the inherited one becomes unobservable. Asking conclude to leave means what stands on the wire is this rung's own work -- reopening leaves the closure standing with no mark, respecting leaves the mark with no closure.
think Dropped a check I had written that compared the standing closure against the inherited one. The two are byte-identical by construction, so the check could only ever have passed for the wrong reason. Better an honest gap than a green line that proves nothing.
think REDS %99's lesson governed the lift. The four bodies were carried into ladder_checks.rye by a transformer that tracks string and comment spans and rewrites identifiers only in code, so no printed sentence or comment could be reached. The harness prose scan then ran and read OK over 370 comments and 925 literals.
obs The measurement falls 1 to 0 -- endings a run opened holding and never named. On the wire the mark reads osrwsmwbyocr: twelve bytes carrying seven tiers, every byte save one from outside this run.
obs The carry did not move. Three births in a row have now left it at 47 lines against a ceiling of 4,000, and the ladder grew to 100 modules and 1,229 checks. Fold C's promise -- a rung costs the ladder only its own checks -- is now proven three times by doing rather than claimed once.
obs The concluding below reads honestly on this pair rather than conveniently: both plans are charged one ending let fall, because both were asked to leave. A number that reads 1 against 1 says the rung below moved under neither plan, which is the truth.
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=94 wall_s=344 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=yes
loom meter=caravan_ladder_copy carried_lines=47 prior=47 modules=100 checks=1229 fold_a=874 fold_b=81 fold_c_stubs=0
loom guard=caravan_ladder_harness_prose comments=370 literals=925 verdict=OK
loom rung=respect measure=unrespected_endings bare=1 under=0 mark_bytes=12 tiers=7
file caravan/respect.rye the rung -- a run that opens holding a closed correspondence names that ending where the outcome is read, and takes the inheritance down
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye takes the four bodies that became identical the moment respect was born -- check_abate_measure, check_abate_wire, check_conclude, check_conclude_refusals
file caravan/conclude.rye gives up those four bodies and stays GREEN, its own measure and wire now the ladder's terminal links
file tools/caravan_respect_witness.rish proves the rung on metal, with a planted control that takes the mark down and makes the closing read again
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the rung so it can never run unheard
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish the meter's fold pins move 835 to 874 and 77 to 81; the carry holds at 47
file caravan/README.md the respect section, and the meter's numbers synced in the same commit as the code
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back at 139d350123 before the operator card's conclude edge folded
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to respect; the conclude edge folds to the condensed pointer
recommend keep-going the correspondence arc now closes and is read: a plan stands a boundary, carries it to a person, hears them, moves on either word they hand back, writes the ending down, and the run after reads it. The next constructive door is the far side of the reading -- a run that has named an inherited ending should carry nobody about that matter again, which is the one claim this rung's prose does not yet make and its code does not yet back. The carry stands at 47 against a ceiling of 4,000, so the ladder still costs a rung nothing but its own checks.
